    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1192">

                <pb facs="0871" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/139</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent Silliman </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-03T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1916, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul Letcher telegraphed Monday. [Here follows telegram from Consul Letcher,
                    dated February 28, 1 p.m.]</p>
                <p>Request appropriate authorities to take steps to punish those guilty of outrages
                    mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
